ause we need also the insects  for also in our environment as well and  they're better if we can control it in  another way rather than using the  poisonous substances time for lunch  besides an environmental focus the farm  also has a social aspect it provides a  home for disabled people  Jehiel works with them in the garden and  also helps them with day-to-day tasks I  had no experience before so I also had  to learn how to work with them in the  Guardian and yeah it's a challenging but  with time you learn how to to have  teamwork you need a lot of patience but  in the long run they are able to work  and deliver results and it helps them at  the farm shop it's a veritable organic  feast cooperation with other organic  farms means that people here have more  than enough to choose from it's  different for sure higher at home water  shortages and disease mean that not  everyone always has enough to eat shahi  has another six months left in Germany  when he gets back home he plans on  starting his own organic farm  I really look forward to having the same  model or bombing in Tanzania and see  whether it will work out about a pink  stripe weight sustainable it's  environmentally friendly living with  nature in producing food with the aim of  maybe more people will come on board and  also to produce enough for everyone  Shahana is sharing his experiences in  Germany he's writing about them in a  blog and if you'd like to know more  about his life as an eco volunteer check  it out DW comm forward slash eco blog

